  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that 10,17-Dioxosparteine may exert its biological effects on HUVEC cells through the activation of Caspase-5, which is a key initiator of apoptosis. This is supported by multiple pathways where 10,17-Dioxosparteine is directly linked to Caspase-5, and Caspase-5 is subsequently targeted by different compounds, including 5-O-Methylcelebixanthone and Lethedioside B, all of which ultimately target HUVEC cells. The scores from these pathways indicate a moderate level of confidence in the relationship between 10,17-Dioxosparteine and HUVEC, suggesting that the observed effects may be mediated through Caspase-5. However, the exact mechanism by which 10,17-Dioxosparteine activates Caspase-5 and leads to HUVEC targeting remains unclear, and further experimental validation would be necessary to confirm the role of these intermediates in the overall biological response.",
